  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is firing on cylinders\u2014MTD revenue up 9% against DOW-adjusted expectation, appointments up 14%, and year-to-date you're at +45% both in dollars and volume. Yesterday was up 1% in total revenue but grooming climbed 5%, which matters more. The concern: add-on attach collapsed from 55% to 41% and retail cratered 25%. This isn't a capacity problem (you ran 7 groomers at $459/groomer, slightly below the 30-day baseline of $490, but bather hours surged to 7.1h vs. 4.8h typical, suggesting the team was doing the work). The signal is operational\u2014your front-of-house team either didn't upsell or didn't retail-push. Hicksville swung the opposite direction: grooming revenue up 36%, add-ons up to 43% attach, but retail tanked 77%. Yesterday was strong relative to capacity (4 groomers, $348/groomer vs. 30-day baseline $407), but month-to-date Hicksville is down 10% against calendar\u2014a real miss despite yesterday's pop. Both stores show the same retail pattern diverging sharply from grooming. That's your one thing to own today: retail discipline.\n\nYou should be proud of Port Washington's year-to-date trajectory and the fact that both locations are running more groomer-days than last month (58 vs. 52 at PW; 26 vs. 28 at HV\u2014Hicksville flat). The lapse pools at both stores ($296k and $91k combined) represent material upside if you activate even 10%.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Today: Port Washington 6 groomers/7.0h bathers, Hicksville 4 groomers/0.0h bathers; next 7 days Port Washington 38 groomer-days, Hicksville 18 groomer-days (front-loaded), and bather hours weighted to PW (43h total)."
